WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.511 --> 00:00:12.680
[children shouting]

2
00:00:24.025 --> 00:00:25.318
[shouting stops]

3
00:00:27.528 --> 00:00:29.197
[girl] <i>This is a true story.</i>

4
00:00:30.364 --> 00:00:33.159
<i>It happened right here
in my town two years ago.</i>

5
00:00:34.452 --> 00:00:37.038
<i>A lot of people die
in a lot of really weird ways</i>

6
00:00:37.121 --> 00:00:38.414
<i>in this story.</i>

7
00:00:38.497 --> 00:00:39.957
<i>but you're not gonna find it
in the news</i>

8
00:00:40.041 --> 00:00:41.626
<i>or anywhere like that</i>

9
00:00:41.709 --> 00:00:44.837
<i>because the police and
the top people in this town</i>

10
00:00:44.921 --> 00:00:46.214
<i>were. like. so embarrassed</i>

11
00:00:46.297 --> 00:00:47.882
<i>that they weren't able
to solve it</i>

12
00:00:47.965 --> 00:00:49.926
<i>that they covered everything
all up.</i>

13
00:00:51.052 --> 00:00:53.512
<i>But if you come here
and ask anyone.</i>

14
00:00:53.596 --> 00:00:54.847
<i>they'll all tell you
the same thing</i>

15
00:00:54.931 --> 00:00:56.891
<i>that I'm gonna tell you now.</i>

16
00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:00.519
<i>This story starts
in my school.</i>

17
00:01:01.979 --> 00:01:03.356
<i>Maybrook Elementary</i>

18
00:01:03.439 --> 00:01:05.650
<i>is kindergarten
through fifth grade.</i>

19
00:01:07.401 --> 00:01:09.153
<i>So this one Wednesday</i>

20
00:01:09.237 --> 00:01:11.864
<i>is like a normal day
for the whole school.</i>

21
00:01:12.698 --> 00:01:15.618
<i>And they had this teacher
who was new.</i>

22
00:01:16.452 --> 00:01:19.121
<i>Her name was Justine Gandy.</i>

23
00:01:20.081 --> 00:01:22.959
<i>And on this day.
she was going to her classroom</i>

24
00:01:23.042 --> 00:01:24.543
<i>just like every morning.</i>

25
00:01:25.753 --> 00:01:27.713
<i>But today was different.</i>

26
00:01:28.673 --> 00:01:31.259
<i>Today. none of her kids
were there.</i>

27
00:01:32.677 --> 00:01:35.972
<i>Every other class at that
school had all their kids.</i>

28
00:01:36.055 --> 00:01:39.475
<i>Even the other third grade
Mrs. Belt taught was full.</i>

29
00:01:40.685 --> 00:01:43.938
<i>But Mrs. Gandy's room
was totally empty.</i>

30
00:01:45.564 --> 00:01:48.276
<i>Well. not totally.</i>

31
00:01:49.443 --> 00:01:51.153
<i>There was one boy there.</i>

32
00:01:51.237 --> 00:01:54.156
<i>And his name was Alex Lilly.</i>

33
00:01:54.907 --> 00:01:58.035
<i>And he was the only kid
in the class of 18</i>

34
00:01:58.119 --> 00:01:59.954
<i>that came to school that day.</i>

35
00:02:01.163 --> 00:02:02.540
<i>And do you know why?</i>

36
00:02:03.582 --> 00:02:05.376
<i>He was the only one there</i>

37
00:02:05.960 --> 00:02:09.880
<i>because the night before
at 2:</i><i>17 in the morning.</i>

38
00:02:09.964 --> 00:02:13.092
<i>every other kid woke up.</i>

39
00:02:13.175 --> 00:02:14.510
<i>got out of bed.</i>

40
00:02:16.429 --> 00:02:17.847
<i>walked downstairs.</i>

41
00:02:19.307 --> 00:02:21.100
<i>opened the front door.</i>

42
00:02:21.183 --> 00:02:24.520
<i>walked across the front yard
and into the dark.</i>

43
00:02:25.479 --> 00:02:28.941
<i>And they never came back.</i>

44
00:02:29.692 --> 00:02:31.527
["Beware of Darkness" playing]

45
00:02:38.951 --> 00:02:40.703
♪ <i>Watch out now</i> ♪

46
00:02:40.786 --> 00:02:46.625
♪ <i>Take care
Beware of falling swingers</i> ♪

47
00:02:51.297 --> 00:02:54.300
♪ <i>Dropping all around you</i> ♪

48
00:02:58.721 --> 00:03:02.308
♪ <i>The pain
That often mingles</i> ♪

49
00:03:03.517 --> 00:03:10.232
♪ <i>In your fingertips</i> ♪

50
00:03:11.442 --> 00:03:15.529
♪ <i>Beware of darkness</i> ♪

51
00:03:22.453 --> 00:03:24.288
♪ <i>Watch out now</i> ♪

52
00:03:24.372 --> 00:03:30.211
<i>♪Take care
Beware of greedy leaders</i> ♪

53
00:03:34.673 --> 00:03:38.177
♪ <i>They take you
Where you should not go</i> ♪

54
00:03:42.264 --> 00:03:46.227
♪ <i>While weeping Atlas cedars</i> ♪

55
00:03:47.103 --> 00:03:50.981
♪ <i>They just want to grow</i> ♪

56
00:03:51.482 --> 00:03:54.276
♪ <i>Grow and grow</i> ♪

57
00:03:54.860 --> 00:03:58.155
♪ <i>Beware of darkness</i> ♪

58
00:03:58.656 --> 00:04:02.243
♪ <i>Beware of darkness...</i> ♪

59
00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:12.211
[girl] <i>All the parents
and people at the school</i>

60
00:04:12.294 --> 00:04:14.255
<i>were really sad and upset.</i>

61
00:04:15.589 --> 00:04:18.717
<i>The police could tell
that the kids left at 2:</i><i>17</i>

62
00:04:19.468 --> 00:04:21.429
<i>because. like. half the houses
had alarms</i>

63
00:04:21.512 --> 00:04:23.764
<i>that got tripped
when they walked outside.</i>

64
00:04:27.268 --> 00:04:29.520
<i>Some of the kids
even got videoed</i>

65
00:04:29.603 --> 00:04:31.105
<i>by the houses
that had cameras.</i>

66
00:04:32.648 --> 00:04:34.483
<i>But the cameras
only showed the kids</i>

67
00:04:34.567 --> 00:04:36.444
<i>walking out into the darkness.</i>

68
00:04:38.446 --> 00:04:40.656
<i>They didn't show
where they went after that.</i>

69
00:04:43.492 --> 00:04:45.494
<i>The police talked
to Alex a lot.</i>

70
00:04:47.371 --> 00:04:50.332
<i>They asked him why his
classmates did what they did.</i>

71
00:04:50.416 --> 00:04:52.209
<i>but he told them
he didn't know.</i>

72
00:04:53.127 --> 00:04:55.212
<i>They asked him
if there was a plan.</i>

73
00:04:55.296 --> 00:04:57.506
<i>but he said if there was.
he never heard it.</i>

74
00:04:58.716 --> 00:05:00.634
<i>They asked him
if there was a TV show</i>

75
00:05:00.718 --> 00:05:02.428
<i>where someone ran away
like that.</i>

76
00:05:03.429 --> 00:05:05.890
<i>but he said if there was.
he never saw it.</i>

77
00:05:07.641 --> 00:05:10.394
<i>They also talked to Mrs. Gandy
a whole bunch.</i>

78
00:05:10.478 --> 00:05:12.104
<i>but she also
didn't know anything</i>

79
00:05:12.188 --> 00:05:13.355
<i>and couldn't help them.</i>

80
00:05:15.149 --> 00:05:16.358
<i>For almost a whole month.</i>

81
00:05:16.442 --> 00:05:19.320
<i>they kept the school closed
for their big investigation.</i>

82
00:05:21.030 --> 00:05:24.033
<i>But after a while. they had to
open everything back up.</i>

83
00:05:24.116 --> 00:05:27.328
<i>so that the kids that didn't
disappear could learn again.</i>

84
00:05:29.121 --> 00:05:30.915
<i>One night before they did.</i>

85
00:05:30.998 --> 00:05:33.167
<i>they had a big meeting
at the school.</i>

86
00:05:34.043 --> 00:05:35.294
<i>There was a bunch
of counselors</i>

87
00:05:35.377 --> 00:05:36.712
<i>and people like that</i>

88
00:05:36.795 --> 00:05:39.256
<i>to help everybody figure out
how to feel</i>

89
00:05:39.340 --> 00:05:41.592
<i>and be sad together. I guess.</i>

90
00:05:44.178 --> 00:05:46.597
<i>This is where the story
really starts.</i>

91
00:05:52.311 --> 00:05:55.439
[man] <i>What's important is
that we don't judge our grief.</i>

92
00:05:55.523 --> 00:05:57.983
We might experience emotions
we don't like.

93
00:05:58.067 --> 00:06:00.027
Emotions besides sadness.

94
00:06:00.986 --> 00:06:03.072
We need to make sure
that we allow ourselves

95
00:06:03.155 --> 00:06:05.157
to feel emotions like anger.

96
00:06:06.283 --> 00:06:10.037
Anger is a very healthy part
of the grief cycle.

97
00:06:10.579 --> 00:06:13.499
It can be especially powerful
in instances of abandonment.

98
00:06:13.582 --> 00:06:15.251
Now. there are often times
that we...

99
00:06:15.334 --> 00:06:16.794
[parent 1]
What does that mean?

100
00:06:16.877 --> 00:06:20.005
"Especially powerful
in instances of abandonment"?

101
00:06:20.089 --> 00:06:22.216
Are you saying that we should
be upset with Matthew?

102
00:06:22.299 --> 00:06:23.592
I'm saying it wouldn't
be abnormal...

103
00:06:23.676 --> 00:06:24.802
[parent 1]
I'll tell you right now

104
00:06:24.885 --> 00:06:26.554
that you may call
what happened "abandonment."

105
00:06:26.637 --> 00:06:28.472
but I don't.
I don't see it like that.

106
00:06:28.556 --> 00:06:32.059
I see something that doesn't
make any sense at all.

107
00:06:32.142 --> 00:06:36.438
We're talking about 17 kids
in one classroom.

108
00:06:36.522 --> 00:06:38.274
What happened
in that classroom?

109
00:06:38.357 --> 00:06:41.026
Why just her classroom?
Why only hers?

110
00:06:41.110 --> 00:06:42.111
- [parent 2] Yeah!
- [others shout]

111
00:06:42.194 --> 00:06:43.571
[counselor] Look. I'm
picking up a lot of emotion.

112
00:06:43.654 --> 00:06:44.488
and that's fine.

113
00:06:44.572 --> 00:06:45.948
[parent 1] So you'll
forgive me if I'm not

114
00:06:46.031 --> 00:06:48.534
particularly interested in
hearing any more out of you.

115
00:06:49.076 --> 00:06:50.828
I wanna hear
from Justine Gandy.

116
00:06:50.911 --> 00:06:51.954
- [parent 2] Yeah.
- [others shout]

117
00:06:52.037 --> 00:06:54.164
[parent 1] She's here.
I wanna know exactly

118
00:06:54.248 --> 00:06:56.083
what she was doing in there.

119
00:06:56.166 --> 00:06:58.168
[overlapping shouting]

120
00:06:59.795 --> 00:07:01.088
[clears throat]

121
00:07:02.673 --> 00:07:03.674
Uh...

122
00:07:05.843 --> 00:07:07.219
I've...

123
00:07:07.303 --> 00:07:08.304
First...

124
00:07:10.097 --> 00:07:15.102
I just wanna say
how very sorry I am for...

125
00:07:15.185 --> 00:07:16.770
all of what's happened.

126
00:07:18.856 --> 00:07:22.860
I know there's nothing
I can say to make this better.

127
00:07:25.779 --> 00:07:27.865
The truth is.
is that I want an answer

128
00:07:27.948 --> 00:07:30.492
- just as bad as all of you.
- [parents shouting]

129
00:07:30.576 --> 00:07:32.828
- [parent 3] Finally. Liar!
- [parent 4] That bitch.

130
00:07:32.911 --> 00:07:34.038
I love those kids.

131
00:07:34.121 --> 00:07:35.122
[parents muttering]

132
00:07:35.205 --> 00:07:36.206
And...

133
00:07:36.290 --> 00:07:38.542
[parents shouting out]

134
00:07:38.626 --> 00:07:39.543
I... I know...

135
00:07:39.627 --> 00:07:41.295
[parent 5]We know you know
exactly what's going on.

136
00:07:41.378 --> 00:07:43.297
I know... I know it's...
it's not...

137
00:07:43.380 --> 00:07:45.633
She should be locked up until
she tells us what happened!

138
00:07:45.716 --> 00:07:47.176
[parents shouting]

139
00:07:48.093 --> 00:07:50.804
Okay. now that kind of thing
is really not called for.

140
00:07:50.888 --> 00:07:52.222
I'm serious.

141
00:07:52.306 --> 00:07:53.223
Mrs. Gandy is here

142
00:07:53.307 --> 00:07:55.517
as an affected member
of this community.

143
00:07:55.601 --> 00:07:56.727
and she is hurting
just like all of us.

144
00:07:56.810 --> 00:07:58.479
[parent 6] You're either
negligent or complicit!

145
00:07:58.562 --> 00:07:59.938
[parents shouting]

146
00:08:01.398 --> 00:08:03.817
[parent 7] Where are
our children. Mrs. Gandy?

147
00:08:03.901 --> 00:08:05.986
That's enough. Everybody needs
to give us some space.

148
00:08:06.070 --> 00:08:08.989
Please. Please.
It's been a long. long night.

149
00:08:09.073 --> 00:08:10.324
We need to get some sleep.

150
00:08:10.407 --> 00:08:12.242
wake up tomorrow
with clearer heads.

151
00:08:12.326 --> 00:08:13.827
[shouting continuing]

152
00:08:13.911 --> 00:08:15.621
Do you have anyone
you can stay with tonight?

153
00:08:15.704 --> 00:08:17.122
- Mm-mmm.
- Then I recommend you going

154
00:08:17.206 --> 00:08:18.540
straight home and laying low.

155
00:08:18.624 --> 00:08:20.292
This feels like
it could turn in...

156
00:08:26.465 --> 00:08:27.716
[person laughing nearby]

157
00:08:32.137 --> 00:08:33.555
[people chatting]

158
00:08:36.100 --> 00:08:37.893
Excuse me. ma'am.
I'm saving up for a bus ticket

159
00:08:37.976 --> 00:08:39.603
to see my brother. Do you have
any change on you at all?

160
00:08:39.687 --> 00:08:41.105
No. I'm sorry. Sorry.

161
00:08:41.188 --> 00:08:42.690
[music playing
through PA system]

162
00:09:16.306 --> 00:09:17.683
[phone buzzing]

163
00:09:24.231 --> 00:09:25.232
Hello?

164
00:09:25.315 --> 00:09:26.358
[heavy breathing on line]

165
00:09:27.484 --> 00:09:28.485
Hello?

166
00:09:29.278 --> 00:09:30.863
[heavy breathing continues]

167
00:09:32.239 --> 00:09:33.991
- Who is this?
- <i>You better watch your back</i>

168
00:09:34.074 --> 00:09:35.576
<i>because tonight's the
night that I...</i>

169
00:09:39.037 --> 00:09:40.622
Excuse me. miss.
I'm saving up for a bus ticket

170
00:09:40.706 --> 00:09:42.166
to see my brother.
Do you have any change?

171
00:09:42.249 --> 00:09:43.876
- No. sorry.
- Okay. thank you.

172
00:09:43.959 --> 00:09:45.878
[people chatting. shouting]

173
00:09:58.682 --> 00:10:00.142
[crickets chirping]

174
00:10:19.536 --> 00:10:20.996
- [bottles clinking]
- [bag thuds]

175
00:10:21.789 --> 00:10:22.873
[Justine exhales]

176
00:10:23.957 --> 00:10:25.709
[people chatting]

177
00:10:30.130 --> 00:10:31.423
[Justine sighs]

178
00:10:31.924 --> 00:10:35.010
<i>Anything the user does.
ZipString follows.</i>

179
00:10:35.719 --> 00:10:38.680
<i>The string flies
at around 35 miles per hour.</i>

180
00:10:38.764 --> 00:10:40.182
<i>and yet is safe to the touch.</i>

181
00:10:40.891 --> 00:10:44.603
<i>All right. Sharks. watch this
trick. It's called the swirl.</i>

182
00:10:46.897 --> 00:10:48.357
<i>This one's the corkscrew.</i>

183
00:10:48.982 --> 00:10:50.108
<i>This one's the step-through.</i>

184
00:10:50.192 --> 00:10:52.152
[doorbell rings]

185
00:10:52.653 --> 00:10:53.946
<i>And pop!</i>

186
00:10:54.738 --> 00:10:56.865
<i>Presenting the portal!</i>

187
00:10:59.868 --> 00:11:01.620
[Austin Hillam]
<i>ZipString glides...</i>

188
00:11:04.414 --> 00:11:05.457
Hello?

189
00:11:20.514 --> 00:11:21.515
Hello?

190
00:11:23.767 --> 00:11:25.060
Yes?

191
00:11:31.859 --> 00:11:33.068
[dog barking]

192
00:11:39.825 --> 00:11:41.743
- [dog barking]
- [Justine panting]

193
00:11:45.664 --> 00:11:46.915
[sighs]

194
00:11:51.044 --> 00:11:52.170
[pounding on door]

195
00:11:52.254 --> 00:11:54.131
- Jesus! Fucking what?
- [pounding stops]

196
00:11:57.384 --> 00:11:58.468
Who's there?

197
00:12:00.762 --> 00:12:01.763
Hello?

198
00:12:09.563 --> 00:12:10.564
Fuck!

199
00:12:15.569 --> 00:12:17.154
[dog barking]

200
00:12:39.301 --> 00:12:40.677
[children playing]

201
00:12:40.761 --> 00:12:42.429
[principal] <i>You're gonna keep
your health insurance.</i>

202
00:12:42.512 --> 00:12:44.264
and if you don't
mind me saying.

203
00:12:45.098 --> 00:12:47.768
there's a lot of mental health
specialists on the plan.

204
00:12:47.851 --> 00:12:48.810
Some of them are...

205
00:12:48.894 --> 00:12:51.855
I. uh...
I just need to work. you know?

206
00:12:51.939 --> 00:12:54.524
I just need to fill my days
with. uh...

207
00:12:56.234 --> 00:12:58.278
Yeah. I... I need to work.
So... [chuckles]

208
00:12:58.904 --> 00:13:01.448
Justine. the scene last night
was just proof

209
00:13:01.531 --> 00:13:04.076
that we have a lot
of emotional parents here.

210
00:13:04.701 --> 00:13:05.786
For now. I think it's best

211
00:13:05.869 --> 00:13:08.205
if you keep some distance
from this place

212
00:13:08.288 --> 00:13:11.124
until folks find time
to sort themselves out.

213
00:13:11.208 --> 00:13:12.918
[child screeching]

214
00:13:13.669 --> 00:13:15.003
How's Alex? Is he...

215
00:13:15.087 --> 00:13:16.421
Alex is doing well.

216
00:13:16.505 --> 00:13:19.383
He's in Mrs. Belt's class.
and we've been advised

217
00:13:19.466 --> 00:13:20.884
that the best thing
that we can do for him

218
00:13:20.968 --> 00:13:23.303
is keep him on a routine.
[inhales]

219
00:13:23.387 --> 00:13:25.305
Keep his life as normal
as possible.

220
00:13:25.389 --> 00:13:26.974
I would like to speak
with him.

221
00:13:27.057 --> 00:13:28.642
We've had this
conversation before.

222
00:13:28.725 --> 00:13:30.185
That's out of the question.

223
00:13:30.268 --> 00:13:32.062
Well. I would...
I would feel so much better

224
00:13:32.145 --> 00:13:33.480
if I could just
speak with him.

225
00:13:33.563 --> 00:13:34.940
- Right there.
- What?

226
00:13:35.023 --> 00:13:37.442
That's the problem.
You'd feel so much better.

227
00:13:37.526 --> 00:13:39.611
He's been scrutinized
by the press.

228
00:13:39.695 --> 00:13:42.030
He's had investigators
ransack his house.

229
00:13:42.114 --> 00:13:43.782
He's been traumatized.

230
00:13:43.865 --> 00:13:46.034
Let's try and put Alex
first. yes?

231
00:13:46.118 --> 00:13:48.537
If you're implying
that I don't care

232
00:13:48.620 --> 00:13:49.955
about Alex. or the students...

233
00:13:50.038 --> 00:13:52.332
The issue isn't you caring
or not caring.

234
00:13:52.416 --> 00:13:54.626
The issue here is.
you have a pattern

235
00:13:54.710 --> 00:13:56.628
in which you overstep
professional lines

236
00:13:56.712 --> 00:13:58.380
- with the students.
- Oh. my God. Here we go.

237
00:13:58.463 --> 00:13:59.464
You know. I do not overstep.

238
00:13:59.548 --> 00:14:01.883
You know it's not appropriate
to hug students.

239
00:14:01.967 --> 00:14:04.845
Oh. I hugged a crying
little boy. Lock me up.

240
00:14:04.928 --> 00:14:07.889
You know driving students home
