00:33:36.807 --> 00:33:38.309
[low chatter]

496
00:33:46.692 --> 00:33:47.693
Mr. Graff.

497
00:33:48.569 --> 00:33:49.570
Yeah.

498
00:33:51.363 --> 00:33:53.449
We follow up on
every one of these calls.

499
00:33:53.532 --> 00:33:55.201
So I can assure you
that as we speak.

500
00:33:55.284 --> 00:33:57.119
we have officers
aggressively pursuing

501
00:33:57.203 --> 00:33:59.121
every lead that comes
through this station.

502
00:33:59.622 --> 00:34:01.498
So. what about the feds?
They got nothing new?

503
00:34:01.582 --> 00:34:04.251
There continues to be a very
healthy information exchange.

504
00:34:04.335 --> 00:34:06.003
So I can tell you
with full confidence

505
00:34:06.086 --> 00:34:09.048
that they are also pursuing
every lead aggressively.

506
00:34:10.341 --> 00:34:11.800
What's happening
with the K-9 units?

507
00:34:11.884 --> 00:34:14.428
I haven't heard about any
K-9 reports in a long time.

508
00:34:14.511 --> 00:34:16.513
That's because
they don't report to you.

509
00:34:18.682 --> 00:34:20.976
Mr. Graff. I can understand
your passion.

510
00:34:21.060 --> 00:34:23.145
And I don't mind having
these conversations with you

511
00:34:23.229 --> 00:34:24.939
because. God forbid.
if it was my child.

512
00:34:25.022 --> 00:34:26.482
I'd be demanding answers too.

513
00:34:26.565 --> 00:34:29.068
But I need you to trust
that what we're doing here...

514
00:34:29.151 --> 00:34:30.527
She's still not talking. huh?

515
00:34:33.447 --> 00:34:34.448
She knows.

516
00:34:34.949 --> 00:34:36.617
I disagree with that.

517
00:34:37.368 --> 00:34:39.995
You're aggressively
following up on every lead.

518
00:34:40.079 --> 00:34:43.374
and yet she's just out there
walking around free as a bird.

519
00:34:43.457 --> 00:34:45.751
Have you done any looking
into her whatsoever?

520
00:34:45.834 --> 00:34:47.253
Extensively. Yes. we have.

521
00:34:47.336 --> 00:34:48.629
So you know about
her past. huh?

522
00:34:48.712 --> 00:34:50.297
'Cause I've done some digging.

523
00:34:50.881 --> 00:34:52.466
And I've found out a lot.

524
00:34:53.092 --> 00:34:56.345
She had a DUI two years ago.
Did you not see that?

525
00:34:56.428 --> 00:34:58.847
She was let go from her
last school that she taught at

526
00:34:58.931 --> 00:35:00.099
for inappropriate behavior.

527
00:35:00.182 --> 00:35:01.600
Did you not see
that one either?

528
00:35:01.684 --> 00:35:03.894
With a member of the faculty.

529
00:35:03.978 --> 00:35:06.146
She's a troubled person.
is she not?

530
00:35:08.274 --> 00:35:10.025
What is it you think
that she knows?

531
00:35:11.694 --> 00:35:13.654
What do you think it is
that she's not telling us?

532
00:35:13.737 --> 00:35:15.406
Because those kids walked out
of those homes.

533
00:35:15.489 --> 00:35:16.699
No one pulled them out.

534
00:35:17.825 --> 00:35:19.285
No one forced them.

535
00:35:19.368 --> 00:35:20.953
I don't see
anything whatsoever

536
00:35:21.036 --> 00:35:22.621
that points to that woman.

537
00:35:25.457 --> 00:35:27.042
What do you see that I don't?

538
00:35:27.835 --> 00:35:30.546
I see something that
I don't understand at all.

539
00:35:30.629 --> 00:35:31.630
[parent 1] Yeah!

540
00:35:31.714 --> 00:35:35.634
We're talking about 17 kids
in one classroom.

541
00:35:35.718 --> 00:35:37.094
And none of them
talked about it?

542
00:35:37.177 --> 00:35:38.053
[parent 2] Exactly.

543
00:35:38.137 --> 00:35:39.555
And we got how many parents
in here.

544
00:35:39.638 --> 00:35:41.223
and none of us saw it coming?

545
00:35:41.307 --> 00:35:42.766
[parents shouting]

546
00:35:42.850 --> 00:35:45.561
I want to know what happened
in that classroom.

547
00:35:45.644 --> 00:35:48.188
Why just her classroom?
Why only hers?

548
00:35:48.272 --> 00:35:50.441
[overlapping voices]

549
00:35:50.524 --> 00:35:51.817
[parent 3]
Where are our children?

550
00:35:51.900 --> 00:35:52.985
[parent 4]
You're just gonna leave?

551
00:35:53.068 --> 00:35:53.902
[Marcus] That's enough.

552
00:35:53.986 --> 00:35:55.195
Everybody needs to give us
some space.

553
00:35:55.279 --> 00:35:56.697
- Please. Please.
- [shouting continuing]

554
00:35:57.239 --> 00:35:59.241
Let's all get
a good night's sleep.

555
00:35:59.325 --> 00:36:00.909
Wake up with clearer heads.
Please.

556
00:36:02.578 --> 00:36:04.371
- [parent 5] She has answers!
- [parents shouting]

557
00:36:09.960 --> 00:36:11.503
[James] Excuse me. miss.
I'm saving up for a bus ticket

558
00:36:11.587 --> 00:36:13.088
to see my brother. Do you have
any change on you at all?

559
00:36:13.172 --> 00:36:14.214
[Justine] Sorry.

560
00:36:47.081 --> 00:36:48.082
[gasps]

561
00:37:19.321 --> 00:37:20.322
Matthew?

562
00:37:35.295 --> 00:37:36.296
Matthew.

563
00:37:38.382 --> 00:37:39.425
[hinge squeaks]

564
00:37:41.844 --> 00:37:43.053
[panting]

565
00:37:49.101 --> 00:37:50.227
Matthew!

566
00:37:53.355 --> 00:37:54.356
Stop!

567
00:38:16.378 --> 00:38:17.379
Wait.

568
00:38:30.851 --> 00:38:32.269
[thunder rumbles]

569
00:38:57.628 --> 00:38:59.755
[footsteps running up stairs]

570
00:39:28.075 --> 00:39:29.076
Matthew?

571
00:40:07.447 --> 00:40:08.448
Matthew?

572
00:40:10.659 --> 00:40:12.077
[gasps]

573
00:40:16.915 --> 00:40:18.250
Matthew. where are you?

574
00:40:22.379 --> 00:40:23.797
Where did you go?

575
00:40:28.677 --> 00:40:29.678
Talk to me.

576
00:40:31.430 --> 00:40:32.598
Talk to me!

577
00:40:39.187 --> 00:40:40.522
[sniffs. groans]

578
00:40:41.815 --> 00:40:42.858
I'm sorry.

579
00:40:44.359 --> 00:40:46.486
I'm sorry that
I wasn't able to sa...

580
00:40:47.738 --> 00:40:48.947
That I wasn't able...

581
00:40:53.535 --> 00:40:55.787
I wanted to say it
so many times.

582
00:40:58.415 --> 00:41:00.167
I really do want to say it
all the time

583
00:41:00.250 --> 00:41:02.586
because I feel it
all the time.

584
00:41:08.467 --> 00:41:09.593
I love you so much.

585
00:41:10.719 --> 00:41:11.720
[shouts]

586
00:41:11.803 --> 00:41:13.472
[grunting. panting]

587
00:41:19.811 --> 00:41:20.979
What the fuck?

588
00:41:51.593 --> 00:41:53.053
Where's our house?

589
00:41:54.096 --> 00:41:55.389
There.

590
00:42:01.478 --> 00:42:05.440
Where's the tower? Tower.
tower. tower. tower. tower.

591
00:42:05.524 --> 00:42:06.858
Ah.

592
00:42:21.415 --> 00:42:22.416
Show me.

593
00:42:24.835 --> 00:42:25.836
Come on.

594
00:42:33.593 --> 00:42:34.803
[bell chiming]

595
00:42:42.477 --> 00:42:43.603
Hi.

596
00:42:43.687 --> 00:42:45.147
- Hello.
- How are you?

597
00:42:46.690 --> 00:42:47.858
I'm Archer Graff.
I'm Matthew's...

598
00:42:47.941 --> 00:42:49.317
Yeah. I know who you are. Hi.

599
00:42:49.401 --> 00:42:52.404
Oh. good. I know we haven't
spoken before directly.

600
00:42:53.071 --> 00:42:54.948
We've seen each other
at a lot of the same...

601
00:42:55.031 --> 00:42:57.576
- How are you. Archer?
- I'm good. I'm real good.

602
00:42:58.368 --> 00:42:59.661
I... You know.

603
00:42:59.745 --> 00:43:01.705
All things considered. just...

604
00:43:02.998 --> 00:43:04.458
soldiering on.

605
00:43:05.375 --> 00:43:06.710
We have to. don't we?

606
00:43:07.210 --> 00:43:08.211
We do.

607
00:43:08.295 --> 00:43:11.298
Listen. I'm sorry to
surprise you at home like this

608
00:43:11.381 --> 00:43:12.799
in the...
in the middle of the day.

609
00:43:12.883 --> 00:43:14.760
But. um. I don't know
if you know.

610
00:43:14.843 --> 00:43:16.970
but we got some footage of
Matthew leaving the house

611
00:43:17.053 --> 00:43:18.889
on our Ring cam thing here.

612
00:43:19.723 --> 00:43:21.892
and I think you folks
had the same...

613
00:43:22.434 --> 00:43:23.977
same situation with Bailey?

614
00:43:24.686 --> 00:43:25.854
Yeah. that's right.

615
00:43:25.937 --> 00:43:28.064
All right. Well. I'm sure
you showed yours to the police

616
00:43:28.148 --> 00:43:30.192
just like I did. but I-I...

617
00:43:31.234 --> 00:43:34.196
I wondered if you would mind
letting me take a look at it.

618
00:43:35.030 --> 00:43:36.156
I don't need a copy
or anything.

619
00:43:36.239 --> 00:43:37.616
I'm not comfortable with that.

620
00:43:42.954 --> 00:43:44.456
Okay. I understand.

621
00:44:06.895 --> 00:44:07.896
Gary?

622
00:44:08.897 --> 00:44:10.273
Archer Graff. How you doing?

623
00:44:10.941 --> 00:44:11.942
Fine.

624
00:44:12.651 --> 00:44:13.944
Matthew's dad.

625
00:44:14.945 --> 00:44:17.030
Yeah. [sighs] Of course.

626
00:44:18.114 --> 00:44:19.115
How's it going?

627
00:44:19.199 --> 00:44:21.952
Um. I have a strange question
I need to ask you.

628
00:44:26.665 --> 00:44:28.208
It's kinda hard to watch this.

629
00:44:28.291 --> 00:44:30.043
Okay. wait. Go back to where
she steps on the sidewalk.

630
00:44:30.126 --> 00:44:31.127
Okay.

631
00:44:31.211 --> 00:44:32.212
Uh...

632
00:44:33.004 --> 00:44:34.923
Okay. Right there.

633
00:44:36.424 --> 00:44:37.467
[Gary] What do you see?

634
00:44:39.094 --> 00:44:41.596
One. two. three. four...

635
00:44:41.680 --> 00:44:45.141
...five. six. seven.

636
00:44:59.364 --> 00:45:00.448
Sorry.

637
00:45:20.886 --> 00:45:22.554
Come on. What am I looking at?

638
00:45:57.380 --> 00:45:58.381
Hey.

639
00:45:59.174 --> 00:46:00.800
- I want to talk to you.
- Well. I...

640
00:46:00.884 --> 00:46:02.761
I don't think we have anything
to say to each other.

641
00:46:02.844 --> 00:46:03.887
I think you have a lot to say.

642
00:46:03.970 --> 00:46:05.972
You and every other person
in this city.

643
00:46:06.056 --> 00:46:08.308
Believe me.
the message is loud and clear.

644
00:46:08.391 --> 00:46:09.851
I'm the problem. Got it.

645
00:46:09.935 --> 00:46:11.061
You know what?
I think that's the first

646
00:46:11.144 --> 00:46:12.687
honest thing
I've heard you say.

647
00:46:12.771 --> 00:46:14.981
- You are the problem.
- You wanna get in my face?

648
00:46:15.065 --> 00:46:16.358
- You wanna threaten me?
- I'm not...

649
00:46:16.441 --> 00:46:17.567
Nobody's threatening you.

650
00:46:17.651 --> 00:46:19.402
You're barking up
the wrong tree. Okay?

651
00:46:19.486 --> 00:46:21.821
This whole victim persona
that you're taking on.

652
00:46:21.905 --> 00:46:23.531
it might have
the police fooled.

653
00:46:23.615 --> 00:46:24.950
it might have
the school fooled...

654
00:46:25.033 --> 00:46:26.451
[speech fades]

655
00:46:28.870 --> 00:46:30.747
- Stop thinking of yourself!
- Marcus?

656
00:46:30.830 --> 00:46:33.041
You and I are gonna
have a conversation right...

657
00:46:33.124 --> 00:46:34.709
- [Marcus grunting]
- [Justine straining]

658
00:46:36.795 --> 00:46:38.254
[Justine gasping]

659
00:46:39.422 --> 00:46:40.423
Hey!

660
00:46:40.507 --> 00:46:42.926
[Marcus babbling incoherently]

661
00:46:46.930 --> 00:46:49.391
- [Marcus snarling]
- [Justine shrieking]

662
00:46:56.982 --> 00:46:58.274
Just stay down.

663
00:46:58.358 --> 00:47:00.318
[panting. growling]

664
00:47:01.444 --> 00:47:02.445
Hey!

665
00:47:05.240 --> 00:47:06.741
[growling]

666
00:47:09.995 --> 00:47:11.830
[snarling]

667
00:47:12.330 --> 00:47:13.331
[shouts. growls]

668
00:47:19.713 --> 00:47:20.880
[shrieking]

669
00:47:26.928 --> 00:47:27.929
[Paul] <i>Hotel's good. though?</i>

670
00:47:28.013 --> 00:47:29.806
- [Donna] <i>It's fine.</i>
- Yeah.

671
00:47:29.889 --> 00:47:32.475
<i>Not the Ritz. but I'm not
expecting them to go nuts.</i>

672
00:47:32.559 --> 00:47:36.229
Yeah. Well. it's only
for six nights. Right?

673
00:47:36.312 --> 00:47:37.564
<i>Three. actually.</i>

674
00:47:37.647 --> 00:47:39.107
<i>Apparently.
I don't have to be here</i>

675
00:47:39.190 --> 00:47:40.358
<i>for the big wrap-up shindig.</i>

676
00:47:40.442 --> 00:47:42.068
<i>so I get to leave on Thursday.</i>

677
00:47:43.486 --> 00:47:45.822
- <i>Isn't that great?</i>
- Yeah. It's good.

678
00:47:45.905 --> 00:47:47.615
<i>'Cause I'm supposed
to ovulate Friday.</i>

679
00:47:47.699 --> 00:47:49.743
<i>so we can hit the target
this month.</i>

680
00:47:51.244 --> 00:47:53.830
Nice. Okay. Yeah. Good.

681
00:47:53.913 --> 00:47:55.540
<i>I thought you'd like that.</i>

682
00:47:55.623 --> 00:47:58.501
<i>Oh. will you tell my dad
when you see him today</i>

683
00:47:58.585 --> 00:47:59.794
<i>that since I'll be back
for the weekend.</i>

684
00:47:59.878 --> 00:48:02.005
<i>we can make their
anniversary lunch thing?</i>

685
00:48:02.088 --> 00:48:03.631
[sighs]
Yeah. I'll let him know.

686
00:48:03.715 --> 00:48:04.883
<i>He'll be happy.</i>

687
00:48:04.966 --> 00:48:06.676
<i>You about to start your shift?</i>

688
00:48:06.760 --> 00:48:07.802
Yep.

689
00:48:07.886 --> 00:48:09.471
<i>You gonna hit
a meeting afterward?</i>

690
00:48:10.430 --> 00:48:12.766
Um. I wasn't planning on it.

691
00:48:14.184 --> 00:48:15.435
<i>Don't you think you should?</i>

692
00:48:16.269 --> 00:48:17.228
[sighs]

693
00:48:17.312 --> 00:48:18.980
Uh. if I have time.
I'll hit one.

694
00:48:19.064 --> 00:48:20.815
<i>Paul. especially when</i>

695
00:48:20.899 --> 00:48:22.400
<i>you're going to be
spending stretches alone.</i>

696
00:48:22.484 --> 00:48:24.903
<i>I think it's important that
you go to regular meetings.</i>

697
00:48:24.986 --> 00:48:27.447
I'm not gonna drink. Donna.
I feel fine.

698
00:48:27.530 --> 00:48:30.658
If I don't feel fine.
then I'll hit a meeting. Okay?

699
00:48:31.284 --> 00:48:32.410
<i>Okay. sweetie.</i>

700
00:48:32.952 --> 00:48:35.080
Okay. I gotta get going now.

701
00:48:35.163 --> 00:48:36.998
<i>Okay. Don't forget to tell
my dad about this weekend.</i>

702
00:48:37.082 --> 00:48:37.999
Yep.

703
00:48:38.083 --> 00:48:39.667
- <i>Love you.</i>
- Love you.

704
00:48:41.836 --> 00:48:43.171
Jesus Christ.

705
00:48:47.217 --> 00:48:48.218
Hey. Ed.

706
00:48:49.177 --> 00:48:50.303
Hey. buddy.

707
00:48:50.386 --> 00:48:51.679
Uh. Donna's back Friday.

708
00:48:51.763 --> 00:48:54.390
so we're good to have lunch
with you guys on Sunday.

709
00:48:54.474 --> 00:48:55.600
Why's she coming back early?

710
00:48:55.683 --> 00:48:57.560
I guess they're
cutting her loose. so...

711
00:48:58.144 --> 00:49:00.855
she wanted me to let you know
that we're in.

712
00:49:02.065 --> 00:49:03.149
Okay. Sounds good.

713
00:49:04.025 --> 00:49:06.361
Anniversary lunch?

714
00:49:07.821 --> 00:49:08.822
Yep.

715
00:49:08.905 --> 00:49:11.116
That's nice.
Well. congratulations and...

716
00:49:11.199 --> 00:49:13.368
- Well. thanks.
- A lot of years.

717
00:49:14.327 --> 00:49:15.787
You calling me old?

718
00:49:15.870 --> 00:49:17.163
No. No. sir. No. no. no.

719
00:49:17.247 --> 00:49:18.289
Why would you call me old?

720
00:49:18.373 --> 00:49:19.707
No. sir. I wasn't saying that.

721
00:49:19.791 --> 00:49:20.875
I'm giving you shit.

722
00:49:22.794 --> 00:49:24.546
Well. just starting
my shift here.

723
00:49:24.629 --> 00:49:25.630
Roger that.

724
00:49:28.424 --> 00:49:29.634
[man talking nearby]

725
00:49:44.774 --> 00:49:46.901
["Don't Be Scared"
playing on radio]

726
00:49:52.031 --> 00:49:53.700
[newsreader] <i>Next Monday
will mark 30 days</i>

727
00:49:53.783 --> 00:49:55.869
<i>since 17 grade-school children
have disappeared</i>

728
00:49:55.952 --> 00:49:56.953
<i>from McCarren County.</i>

729
00:49:57.036 --> 00:49:59.247
<i>Community members
have issued a $50.000 reward</i>

730
00:49:59.330 --> 00:50:01.332
<i>for any information
leading to their recovery.</i>

731
00:50:01.416 --> 00:50:03.084
<i>Any suspicious individual
or activity</i>

732
00:50:03.168 --> 00:50:04.210
<i>should be reported to your...</i>

733
00:50:04.294 --> 00:50:05.378
[radio off]

734
00:50:16.890 --> 00:50:19.184
- [single-tone siren]
- Stop right there. Police.

735
00:50:22.187 --> 00:50:23.271
Shit.

736
00:50:24.647 --> 00:50:26.858
[siren wailing]

737
00:50:45.210 --> 00:50:46.711
[truck horn blares]

738
00:51:04.646 --> 00:51:06.272
Stop or you're gonna
get the Taser!

739
00:51:08.566 --> 00:51:10.151
[groaning]

740
00:51:10.235 --> 00:51:12.070
Dude. please.
Stop. Stop. Stop. Stop.

741
00:51:12.153 --> 00:51:14.113
- Shut up.
- Please. I work there. man.

742
00:51:14.197 --> 00:51:16.950
I just lost my keys. Please.

743
00:51:18.243 --> 00:51:19.911
I lost my keys. Please.

744
00:51:19.994 --> 00:51:21.287
[man groaning]

745
00:51:21.371 --> 00:51:23.581
- You okay?
- Yes. Officer. I'm okay.

746
00:51:23.665 --> 00:51:25.416
All right. We went down
pretty hard there. You good?

747
00:51:25.500 --> 00:51:27.669
Officer. I'm okay.
Just please call my warehouse.

748
00:51:27.752 --> 00:51:28.920
You can look the number
up online.

749
00:51:29.003 --> 00:51:30.213
My phone isn't working
right now.

750
00:51:30.296 --> 00:51:31.714
